/**
 * Home Orbit's privacy policy, written 10 October 2026 from how the platform actually handles
 * shoppers' data (docs/14 "Personal data", docs/18). It is our draft for Home Orbit: their lawyer
 * should review it before launch (docs/14: the DPDP Rules' notice duties apply in full from
 * 13 May 2027). Format for outlineToLexical: "## " headings, "- " bullets, other lines paragraphs.
 */
export const PRIVACY_POLICY = `
Last updated: 10 October 2026

This policy explains what personal data Home Orbit collects when you use this website, why we collect it, who we share it with and the choices you have. Home Orbit decides how your data is used (under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, we are the Data Fiduciary). Our online store runs on a software platform that processes data only on our instructions.

## What we collect
- Contact details you give us: your name, mobile number, email address and, for deliveries, your address and pincode.
- Business details if you buy for a business or ask for a bulk quote: company name and GSTIN.
- Orders and requests: the products you order or ask about, quantities, quote requests and messages you send us.
- Payment status: whether a payment succeeded and its reference. Card, UPI and bank details are entered on our payment partner's page; we never see or store them.
- Reviews you choose to write, with the name you want shown.
- Technical data needed to run the store: cookies that keep your cart, sign-in and wishlist working, and basic records of visits used to keep the store secure.

## Why we use it
- To process your order, deliver it, send you a GST invoice and handle returns, refunds and warranty claims.
- To answer your enquiries and send the quotes you ask for.
- To send you order updates (confirmation, dispatch, delivery) by email, SMS or WhatsApp on the number you gave for that order.
- To send offers and news of new designs, only if you tick the box for that channel. These boxes are never ticked for you.
- To keep the store safe, prevent fraud and meet our legal duties, such as keeping tax records.

We collect only what we need for these purposes and do not use your data for anything else.

## Who we share it with
- Courier and shipping partners, to deliver your order (your name, phone and address).
- Our payment partner, to take your payment securely.
- Email, SMS and WhatsApp service providers, to send the messages described above.
- Our e-commerce platform provider, which hosts the store and processes data on our behalf only.
- Government or legal authorities, when the law requires it.

We do not sell your personal data, and we do not share it with anyone for their own advertising.

## How long we keep it
- Order records and invoices: for as long as tax and accounting laws require (currently up to eight years), with other personal details kept to a minimum.
- Carts that are not checked out: 30 days. Sign-in sessions: 30 days. One-time sign-in codes: 10 minutes.
- Enquiries and messages: as long as needed to answer them and follow up.
- Message logs: 90 days.

## Your choices and rights
- See and correct your details: sign in to My account and edit your profile and addresses.
- Ask us for a copy of your data, or ask us to delete your account. When an account is deleted, we keep only the order and invoice records the law requires.
- Stop offer messages at any time: use the unsubscribe link in any offer message, the unsubscribe page, or your account settings. Order updates never carry offers.
- Stop WhatsApp or SMS order updates: reply STOP, or use the order tracking page or your account settings.
- Withdraw any consent you gave, as easily as you gave it. This does not affect what we did before you withdrew it.
- Nominate someone to use these rights for you if you are unable to.

To use any of these rights, contact us using the details on our Contact page.

## Cookies
We use cookies that the store needs to work: your cart, your sign-in, your saved wishlist and to keep forms safe. Your recent searches and recently viewed products are kept only in your own browser.

## Security
Data is sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). Access to customer data is limited to the staff who need it, and payment details are handled by our payment partner. If a breach affecting your data occurs, we will inform you and the authorities as the law requires.

## Children
This store is meant for adults. If you are under 18, please use it with a parent or guardian.

## Grievances
If you have a concern about your data or this policy, write to our grievance officer. Their name and contact details are on our Contact page and at the foot of every page. We acknowledge complaints within 48 hours and aim to resolve them within one month. You may also approach the Data Protection Board of India.

## Changes to this policy
We will post any change on this page with a new date. If a change affects how we use data you have already given us, we will tell you before it applies.
`
